│ patch_description        │ Replace the weak random greedy/SA with a construction exploiting the known extremal       │
│                          │ trade-off: a dense interval (small sum set, moderate difference set) combined with a      │
│                          │ Golomb-like sparse part (large difference set, controlled sum set). We add:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. A fast incremental scorer using dicts of sum/diff counts so we can evaluate candidate  │
│                          │ additions cheaply (O(n) per candidate instead of O(n^2)).                                 │
│                          │ 2. A proper Golomb-ruler greedy builder that produces near-optimal difference sets.       │
│                          │ 3. A "dense core + Golomb offset" construction parameterized by (m, gs, gap) which is the │
│                          │ main lever: core {0..m} gives |A+A| ≈ 2m+1 while the Golomb tail adds ~gs^2 distinct      │
│                          │ differences without blowing up the sum set too much.                                      │
│                          │ 4. A targeted SA that mutates by add/drop/perturb around this structured seed, with the   │
│                          │ fast scorer, so many more iterations fit in the budget.                                   │
│                          │ 5. Explicit systematic scan over small (m, gs, gap) which is where the optimum is known   │
│                          │ to sit for this ratio.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should push log|A-A|/log|A+A| from ~1.14 toward the ~1.28 best-known regime.         │
