│                          │ with small sum set but large difference set are related to Sidon/B_h sets and Golomb      │
│                          │ rulers. In particular, for a Golomb ruler the difference set has all distinct positive    │
│                          │ values (|A-A| = n(n-1)+1, the maximum possible), giving log|A-A| ≈ 2 log n. Meanwhile, we │
│                          │ can choose the ruler so that A+A is small.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A strong known family is the "Singer difference set" / modular Sidon construction: take a │
│                          │ Sidon set S in Z_p (a perfect difference set of size q+1 when p = q^2+q+1), then the      │
│                          │ difference set covers all nonzero residues (|A-A| = p) while the sum set in integers can  │
│                          │ be kept small. Concretely, a Bose-Chowla Sidon set of size q+1 in Z_{q^2-1} has the       │
│                          │ property that all differences are distinct mod q^2-1, but as integers the set             │
│                          │ {0,1,3,7,...} (powers-of-2-like Sidon) is a classic example.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I'll implement a constructive approach: build a Sidon set via the Bose-Chowla             │
│                          │ construction using a finite field, then map it to integers. This guarantees |A-A| ≈ n^2   │
│                          │ (near-maximal) while giving control over |A+A|. I'll also add a local-search polish step  │
│                          │ on top of the construction to reduce |A+A| further without breaking the difference-set    │
│                          │ size.                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Concretely:                                                                               │
│                          │ - Use the classic Sidon set {2^(2^i)} style? No — better: use the Erdos-Turan / Bose      │
│                          │ construction: for prime power q, the set { (x, x^2) mapped } gives Sidon. Simplest        │
│                          │ practical: pick a Sidon set of integers directly via a greedy Golomb-ruler-like           │
│                          │ construction that maximizes |A-A| and then run local search minimizing |A+A|.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I'll build a set whose difference set is essentially all distinct (Golomb ruler) — e.g. a │
│                          │ known optimal Golomb ruler of order ~25 — which gives |A-A| = n(n-1)+1. Then apply local  │
│                          │ search that only accepts moves reducing |A+A| (while keeping the difference set large).   │
│                          │ This should push the ratio well above 1.14 toward ~1.28.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Implementation plan:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Construct a Golomb ruler greedily: start with {0}, repeatedly add the smallest integer │
│                          │ that keeps all pairwise differences distinct.                                             │
│                          │ 2. Compute initial score.                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Run local search that perturbs elements to reduce |A+A| while maintaining |A-A| close  │
│                          │ to n(n-1)+1 (accept moves that increase the ratio).                                       │
│                          │ 4. Increase time budget and set size (Golomb rulers of order 20-30 give large ratios).    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I'll replace the whole solve() with this construction + targeted local search, and boost  │
│                          │ the deadline to ~100s.                                                                    │
