│ patch_description        │ The original program relies on greedy construction and simulated annealing with weak      │
│                          │ structural priors (random perturbations of small integers). The key parameters are the    │
│                          │ set size n, the candidate range hi, the swap/mutation rates, and the cooling schedule.    │
│                          │ The new approach replaces these with a hybrid construction that explicitly maximizes the  │
│                          │ difference-set-to-sum-set ratio using Golomb-rule-like structures embedded in a dense     │
│                          │ interval. Specifically:                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Use a dense core {0..m} which gives a large number of small sums (few distinct sums     │
│                          │ relative to size), and add Golomb-ruler-like marks offset far away to boost the number of │
│                          │ distinct differences without increasing sums proportionally.                              │
│                          │ - Replace random local search with a targeted "difference-maximizing" greedy: each new    │
│                          │ element is chosen to maximize new distinct differences while keeping new sums minimal.    │
│                          │ - Use a much larger candidate pool derived from existing pairwise differences and sums,   │
│                          │ which is the key structural insight for ratio optimization.                               │
│                          │ - Add a multi-restart mechanism using different (m, golomb_size, gap) configurations,     │
│                          │ sweeping parameters more finely than the original.                                        │
│                          │ - Keep a fast incremental scoring function to evaluate candidates within the time budget. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This explicitly targets the objective log|A-A|/log|A+A| rather than generic set search,   │
│                          │ and should push the ratio above 1.2.                                                      │
