╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ simanneal_restart_sidon                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The previous programs plateau around sum-difference score 1.137 with a combined score of  │
│                          │ 0.89. The feedback explicitly blamed the low non-improving acceptance probability         │
│                          │ (0.02–0.03) for restricted exploration, yet the best program barely raised it. My rewrite │
│                          │ addresses this directly:                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Higher and annealed acceptance probability.** I raise the SA acceptance rate to      │
│                          │ ~0.12 early, annealed geometrically down to ~0.001. This lets the search escape local     │
│                          │ optima while still converging.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Periodic restarts from the strongest seed family.** The dense-core + Golomb          │
│                          │ ("bounded Sidon") construction is the best-performing structured seed. I add a restart    │
│                          │ loop that re-seeds from this family whenever no improvement is seen for ~20 seconds.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Better seed diversity.** I add bounded Sidon-set seeds using the classic `{i*m +     │
│                          │ (i*i mod m)}` construction, which is known to give near-optimal |A-A| for small sets      │
│                          │ while keeping |A+A| small. These are combined with dense cores and Golomb offsets.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Faster incremental scoring.** I keep a set-based diff/sum computation but avoid      │
│                          │ recomputing full O(n²) score on every candidate by only recomputing when the size changes │
│                          │ significantly.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Temperature schedule + stagnation restart.** T drops by a factor each 1500 steps;    │
│                          │ after 20 s without improvement, the current state is reset to the best seed and T is      │
│                          │ bumped back up.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result is a search that explores more aggressively early and exploits the best        │
│                          │ structured seeds late, matching the recommendations without changing the input/output     │
│                          │ contract.                                                                                 │
