├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_reflection_polish                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The existing `_reflect_half` operation is a difference-preserving, sum-altering           │
│                          │ structural move: reflecting a subset of A around some center c preserves the difference   │
│                          │ set structure (up to sign) while potentially shrinking the sum set. Currently it is only  │
│                          │ applied once with the midpoint of the full set and only to the top half.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I will generalize this into a `_reflect_fraction(A, frac, center_mode)` helper that       │
│                          │ enumerates several reflection centers and reflection fractions (top 30%, 40%, 50%), plus  │
│                          │ alternative centers (midpoint, mean, median, and the midpoint of the top portion). For    │
│                          │ each candidate we evaluate `_score`, keeping the best. This is cheap because reflection   │
│                          │ is O(n) and scoring is O(n^2), so trying ~12 variants per set is negligible compared to   │
│                          │ the 100s local search.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I will apply this multi-reflection polish:                                                │
│                          │ 1. To each structured seed (quadratic constructions and bounded Sidon sets) so that seeds │
│                          │ are improved before local search begins.                                                  │
│                          │ 2. As a stronger final polish on the best set found, iterating the best reflection a few  │
│                          │ times until no improvement (since reflection can be applied repeatedly and each           │
│                          │ application can further reduce |A+A|).                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly targets the ratio log|A−A|/log|A+A| by shrinking the denominator without    │
│                          │ touching the numerator.                                                                   │
