│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_cardinality_search                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a fixed-size local search seeded by a handful of structured      │
│                          │ constructions, and the score includes a tiny size bonus `(1 - 1/len(a))/100`. The         │
│                          │ recommendation is to replace this negligible bonus with a cardinality-aware search that   │
│                          │ optimizes `n` jointly. I will:                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Remove the size bonus from `_score`, making it the pure log-ratio (so cardinality      │
│                          │ changes are not artificially rewarded).                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Add a `_local_search(A, deadline, rng)` helper that runs the perturbation loop for a   │
│                          │ given starting set, returning the best found.                                             │
│                          │ 3. In `solve`, run `_local_search` across a range of cardinalities (n ∈ {60, 100, 150,    │
│                          │ 200, 300}) using structured seeds (quadratic sets, bounded Sidon sets, greedy Sidon sets) │
│                          │ of matching sizes, plus the current best as a warm start.                                 │
│                          │ 4. Also add a "delete/insert" move to the local search so n can drift within a run,       │
│                          │ allowing the search to find the best cardinality automatically.                           │
│                          │ 5. Report which n maximizes the pure ratio by tracking the best over all runs.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should let the search explore larger n where |A+A| may grow sub-quadratically (e.g.  │
│                          │ Sidon-like sets have |A+A| ~ n²/2 but the ratio still depends on structure), and avoid    │
│                          │ wasting effort on the size bonus.                                                         │
