│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best features of both prior programs. From the first program, │
│                          │ it preserves the efficient `_greedy_golomb` construction with `used_diffs` tracking and   │
│                          │ the `_incremental_score` fast scoring. From the second program, it keeps the              │
│                          │ `_score_fast` and additional construction variety. The main improvements are: (1) using   │
│                          │ the faster `_incremental_score` everywhere instead of the full O(n^2) `_score` in the     │
│                          │ inner loop, (2) a more focused phase-1 sweep with early termination, (3) an improved      │
│                          │ local search based on the first program's `_refine` which uses targeted moves             │
│                          │ (difference-based moves, add via reflection, pop, swap) that better explore the           │
│                          │ sum/difference tradeoff, and (4) a final polish phase that tries to grow the set by       │
│                          │ adding elements that maximize new differences while minimizing new sums. The result keeps │
│                          │ the same `solve()` interface and returns a sorted list of distinct integers.              │
