│ patch_name               │ difference_set_sidon_solver                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This approach abandons stochastic local search on the full objective and instead exploits │
│                          │ the exact combinatorial structure of the problem. The key insight: to maximize            │
│                          │ log|A−A|/log|A+A| we want a set whose difference set is as close to a Sidon set (all      │
│                          │ pairwise differences distinct) as possible, while its sum set is as small as possible.    │
│                          │ The best known constructions combine:                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. A **Sidon-like core** built via a fast backtracking / greedy search that greedily      │
│                          │ maximizes new differences per added element (not the full objective), producing           │
│                          │ near-perfect Golomb rulers.                                                               │
│                          │ 2. A **sum-collapsing trick**: instead of a plain dense interval (whose sum set is huge), │
│                          │ we use a *geometric/progression* base that keeps A+A small by making many sums coincide   │
│                          │ (e.g. A = {0,1,2,...,m} ∪ {large offsets} — the dense part itself has small sum set       │
│                          │ relative to size).                                                                        │
│                          │ 3. **Exact incremental evaluation** using sorted arrays and bitset-like difference        │
│                          │ tracking, so we can afford many more evaluations than the previous implementation.        │
│                          │ 4. **Deterministic multi-seed restart** with a diversified portfolio of structured seeds  │
│                          │ (pure Golomb, dense + Golomb, powers-of-two-like, Sidon-set-from-prime-field) rather than │
│                          │ random SA.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The crucial change is the search objective: instead of SA on log|A−A|/log|A+A| directly   │
│                          │ (which is noisy and stuck), we do **greedy difference-maximization with sum-cost          │
│                          │ penalty**, evaluated exactly, then only accept additions that strictly improve the ratio. │
│                          │ This matches the underlying combinatorial structure and should push the ratio             │
│                          │ substantially above 1.137.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, we use **B_h set constructions from finite fields** (Singer difference      │
│                          │ sets) as seeds — these are known to have near-optimal difference/sum ratios for their     │
│                          │ size.                                                                                     │
