├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sum_set_compaction_move                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current local search perturbs elements randomly and only accepts moves based on the   │
│                          │ full log-ratio score. Prior feedback indicates the binding constraint is the denominator  │
│                          │ (|A+A|), not the numerator. This edit adds a targeted "sum-set compaction" move to        │
│                          │ `_local_search` that directly attacks |A+A|:                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For a randomly chosen index i, we compute the base diff/sum sets once, then try candidate │
│                          │ replacement values v in a small window around a (say ±30). For each v we cheaply estimate │
│                          │ the new sum set size as |base_sums ∪ {v + z : z in A\{a}} ∪ {2v}| and the new diff set    │
│                          │ size similarly, then accept the v that minimizes |new_sums| subject to |new_diffs| >=     │
│                          │ 0.95 * |base_diffs|. This is O(window * n) per move instead of a full O(n^2) recompute    │
│                          │ per candidate, and it explicitly optimizes the denominator.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ We integrate this as a new move branch in the existing random-move selection with a       │
│                          │ modest probability (~0.10), keeping the existing moves for exploration. When the          │
│                          │ compaction move is chosen, we perform the window scan, pick the best v, and use it as the │
│                          │ candidate. This directly reduces |A+A| while preserving most of |A-A|, improving          │
│                          │ log|A-A|/log|A+A|.                                                                        │
