╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ratio_aware_topk_seed_selection                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program spends its entire Phase 1 budget (~25s) enumerating structured seeds  │
│                          │ and only tracks a single `best` seed by the full score (which includes the small size     │
│                          │ bonus). This means it often starts refinement from the first seed that happens to beat    │
│                          │ the incumbent, rather than from the seed with the highest *pure* log-ratio (which is what │
│                          │ actually drives the objective).                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Idea: instead of greedily keeping only one seed, collect the top-K (K=8) seeds ranked by  │
│                          │ their pure `log|A-A|/log|A+A|` (excluding the size bonus), then run the local-search      │
│                          │ refinement from each of these K seeds in order within the remaining budget. This is the   │
│                          │ recommendation from the feedback: rank by the pure log-ratio, and use the size bonus only │
│                          │ as a tiebreaker.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Implementation:                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Add a `_score_pure(a)` helper that returns `log|A-A|/log|A+A|` without the size bonus. │
│                          │ 2. In Phase 1, maintain a small priority list `top_seeds` of (pure_score, cand) keeping   │
│                          │ the top K=8 unique candidates.                                                            │
│                          │ 3. In Phase 2/3, iterate over `top_seeds` (sorted descending by pure score) and run       │
│                          │ `_local_search` from each, within the remaining budget, keeping the overall best by full  │
│                          │ score.                                                                                    │
│                          │ 4. Keep the existing random-restart loop for the leftover budget after refining all top-K │
│                          │ seeds.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves the existing structure and only changes the seed selection strategy to be  │
│                          │ ratio-aware and diverse.                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0000                                                                                   │
