│ patch_description        │ The current `solve()` only performs a single-scale local search that perturbs one element │
│                          │ at a time. The recommendation points out that the growth phase is one-shot and cannot     │
│                          │ escape the basin of its seed. I will extend the local search to also include an iterative │
│                          │ growth/refinement phase that:                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Allows multi-step non-improving additions (soft revert with epsilon tolerance) so that │
│                          │ the search can traverse valleys.                                                          │
│                          │ 2. Sweeps a tradeoff weight `w ∈ {0.15, 0.25, 0.35, 0.5}` in a custom gain function `gain │
│                          │ = d_gain - w * s_cost` where `d_gain` is the change in |A-A| and `s_cost` is the change   │
│                          │ in |A+A|. This directly targets the ratio by exploring the Pareto frontier between        │
│                          │ differences and sums.                                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Runs several restarts from the best structured seeds found so far.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a targeted change to the local-search loop only, keeping all existing             │
│                          │ constructions intact. It should improve the sum-difference score by finding sets with     │
│                          │ better tradeoffs that single-element perturbation cannot reach.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The change is localized: modify the local search section of `solve()` to add an iterative │
│                          │ growth phase with weight sweep and soft revert, and add a helper `_growth_search`         │
