├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ spectral_sidon_anneal                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs rely on dense-core + Golomb/Sidon constructions and SA over raw        │
│                          │ element moves. Key insight: the ratio log|A-A|/log|A+A| is maximized when the sum-set is  │
│                          │ nearly as small as possible relative to a near-Sidon difference set. Sidon sets (all      │
│                          │ pairwise sums mostly distinct) give |A+A| ~ n^2/2 while still having |A-A| ~ n^2, but     │
│                          │ they are hard to construct greedily at scale.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach: build a **multiscale Sidon-like seed** using the classical Bose-Chowla /  │
│                          │ Erdős–Turán construction modulo a prime, then apply a **reflection-and-shift polish       │
│                          │ operator** that (a) reflects a suffix of the set around a chosen center to preserve the   │
│                          │ difference multiset structure while collapsing sum collisions, and (b) performs a         │
│                          │ targeted "sum-collision repair" step that only accepts moves strictly reducing |A+A|      │
│                          │ while keeping |A-A| within 99% of its peak. This is fundamentally different from raw SA:  │
│                          │ it uses algebraic seeds and a structural polish operator rather than random element       │
│                          │ perturbations.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The Bose-Chowla construction: for prime p, A = { 2p*i + (i^2 mod p) : i = 0..p-1 } gives  │
│                          │ a Sidon set of size p in [0, 2p^2). We sweep p over primes, then polish with              │
│                          │ reflection/shift operators and a light SA fallback.                                       │
