│ patch_description        │ The current program spends a large amount of time exhaustively enumerating Sidon          │
│                          │ constructions (quadratic sets, bounded Sidon sets, greedy Sidon sets) and keeps only the  │
│                          │ single best seed by the combined score (which includes the small size bonus). This wastes │
│                          │ the exploration of many nearly-equivalent configurations and gives only one starting      │
│                          │ point for the 100-second local search.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to:                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Separate the pure ratio `log|A-A|/log|A+A|` from the size bonus during seed selection, │
│                          │ so seeds are ranked by the primary objective.                                             │
│                          │ 2. Collect the top-K (K≈20) distinct seeds by pure ratio instead of just the single best. │
│                          │ 3. Run local search sequentially over these top-K seeds within the remaining time budget  │
│                          │ (still respecting the 110s deadline), so the highest-ratio seed gets the most refinement  │
│                          │ time, and diverse basins are explored.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the existing seed generators (quadratic, bounded Sidon, greedy Sidon) but      │
│                          │ changes the selection/refinement loop to be ratio-aware and top-K based. The size bonus   │
│                          │ is retained only as a tiebreaker.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Implementation details:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Add a helper `_ratio(a)` that returns the pure log-ratio (or -inf for degenerate sets). │
│                          │ - Maintain a list `seeds` of (ratio, a) tuples collected from every generator.            │
│                          │ - After generation, deduplicate seeds (by frozenset) and keep the top-K by ratio.         │
│                          │ - Loop over the top-K seeds, allocating a share of the remaining time to each (e.g.,      │
│                          │ proportional to rank), running the existing local search from each seed and tracking the  │
│                          │ best overall by `_score`.                                                                 │
│                          │ - Keep the final polishing step on the overall best.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This targets the plateau at 1.13731 by starting refinement from the highest-ratio         │
│                          │ configurations rather than the first improving one, and by exploring multiple basins.     │
