╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ratio_aware_seed_topk_parallel_refine                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign of the search architecture:                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Ratio-aware seed ranking (no size bonus in selection).** Phase 1 now enumerates a    │
│                          │ broad family of structured seeds (dense cores, strided cores, scaled Golomb tails,        │
│                          │ product-like mixed constructions) and scores them by the *pure* ratio R =                 │
│                          │ log|A-A|/log|A+A|. The (1-1/n)/100 bonus is only used as a final tiebreaker. The top-K    │
│                          │ (K≈24) seeds are retained rather than the single best.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Diverse seed-family portfolio.** Adds new structural families that often beat plain  │
│                          │ dense+Golomb: (a) strided dense cores with stride 2/3/4, (b) scaled Golomb tails with     │
│                          │ scale 1..4, (c) "two-block" constructions where a dense block and a scaled Golomb block   │
│                          │ are placed far apart to enlarge the difference set while keeping sums in two clusters,    │
│                          │ and (d) small pure intervals which are strong at small n.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Parallel-style round-robin refinement.** Instead of committing all remaining budget  │
│                          │ to one seed, we run short refinement bursts cycling through the top-K seeds. Each burst   │
│                          │ is a short SA pass; we track the global best across all bursts. This guards against local │
│                          │ basins and matches the recommendation to refine top-K "in parallel order."                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Fast incremental scorer.** A single O(n^2) symmetric scorer using i<=j loops with    │
│                          │ both signs of the difference and both sums added once. All other helpers call into this   │
│                          │ single scorer to avoid duplication.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Greedy growth polish** kept but tightened: it only adds elements that strictly       │
│                          │ increase the pure ratio, and reverts if not.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 6. **Time-budgeted phases** with explicit deadlines so the program always returns within  │
│                          │ the 110s window.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The overall data-flow is: generate → score by pure ratio → top-K → round-robin short      │
│                          │ refinements → greedy polish → return.                                                     │
