                        Patch Metadata - Gen 32/1000 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                        
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ diversity_seed_augmentation                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The bottleneck identified in prior generations is seed structure, not refinement. The     │
│                          │ current program relies on a single best seed for local search (Phase 2) and random        │
│                          │ structured restarts (Phase 3). This wastes the fact that `_reflect_half`-style            │
│                          │ transformations (negating/reflecting a subset of marks) preserve the difference-set size  │
│                          │ almost exactly while producing structurally distinct seeds with the same cardinality.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I add a `_reflect_marks` helper that reflects a subset of marks (the top fraction of      │
│                          │ marks above a center) around a chosen center. This is a cardinality-preserving, roughly   │
│                          │ difference-preserving transformation. After Phase 1 selects the top-K structured seeds,   │
│                          │ we generate 3-5 reflected variants per top seed (using multiple centers/fractions), keep  │
│                          │ only distinct-cardinality outputs, and feed each into `_local_search`. This gives genuine │
│                          │ basin diversity at near-zero cost.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I also restructure Phase 1 to keep a top-K list of seeds (not just the single best) so    │
│                          │ reflected variants can be derived from several strong starting points, and I add the      │
│                          │ reflected variants into the restart pool in Phase 3.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Concretely:                                                                               │
│                          │ - Add `_reflect_marks(a, center, frac)` helper.                                           │
│                          │ - In Phase 1, collect a `top_seeds` list (top-8 distinct by score).                       │
│                          │ - After Phase 1, generate reflected variants of each top seed at centers {0.3, 0.4, 0.5,  │
│                          │ 0.6, 0.7} of the span and fractions {0.3, 0.4, 0.5} of the top marks; dedupe by           │
│                          │ cardinality; run `_local_search` on each within the remaining budget.                     │
│                          │ - In Phase 3, occasionally seed from a reflected variant of the current best instead of a │
│                          │ fresh dense+Golomb construction.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a targeted, low-risk change: it only adds new seed-generation code paths and does │
│                          │ not modify the objective or the core search operators.                                    │
