│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ratio_aware_multibasin_growth                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign around three ideas:                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Single symmetric fast scorer** used everywhere (avoids the redundant double-loop in  │
│                          │ the current `_diff_sum_sets` which iterates `j in range(n)` and adds both `ai-aj` and     │
│                          │ `aj-ai`; use `j in range(i,n)` plus both signs). This is roughly a 2x speedup of every    │
│                          │ inner loop and lets us do more search in the same budget.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Ratio-aware top-K seed collector replaces the fixed Phase-1 sweep.** Instead of      │
│                          │ scoring and immediately discarding, we enumerate the Bose-Chowla family (plus             │
│                          │ scaled/reflected variants) and *all* small structured seeds, rank them by PURE            │
│                          │ `log|A-A|/log|A+A|`, and keep the top K=20. The insight from Gen 26 is that the value is  │
│                          │ in starting refinement from the highest-ratio basin; the size bonus is only a tiebreaker. │
│                          │ This frees ~30s previously consumed by an exhaustive sweep and feeds the refinement phase │
│                          │ with the strongest basins.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Round-robin short SA bursts across the top-K seeds.** Rather than polishing each     │
│                          │ seed for a fixed 3s and then moving on, we cycle through the top-K with short (≈3s)       │
│                          │ bursts, so the highest-ratio basins get revisited repeatedly as the budget shrinks. A     │
│                          │ greedy growth polish on the global best is applied at the end, using a difference-gain /  │
│                          │ sum-cost heuristic as in the prior version that reached 1.137.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The overall architecture is: scorer → seed bank → ratio-ranked top-K → round-robin SA     │
│                          │ bursts → greedy growth polish → return. This keeps the Bose-Chowla Sidon structural prior │
│                          │ (which is what actually produces the good ratios), but reorganizes the control flow so    │
│                          │ search time is spent on the best basins rather than in an exhaustive enumeration phase.   │
