                        Patch Metadata - Gen 37/1000 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                        
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ diverse_seed_bank_growth                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program's bottleneck is seed structure and diversity: it refines a small set  │
│                          │ of top-K seeds (ranked by pure log-ratio) but the seeds are structurally similar          │
│                          │ (dense-core + Sidon/Golomb) and reflection (a near-score-preserving,                      │
│                          │ difference-preserving operation) is not exploited for seed diversity. Key parameters      │
│                          │ changed/added:                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Reflection-based seed augmentation** (new): after building the top-K, generate 3-5   │
│                          │ reflected variants of the best seed at multiple centers {0.3, 0.4, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7} of the  │
│                          │ span and fractions {0.3, 0.4, 0.5} of the marks. Keep only distinct-cardinality outputs,  │
│                          │ re-rank by pure ratio, and merge into the bank. This gives genuine basin diversity at     │
│                          │ near-zero cost.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Larger K** (8 -> 24) so reflected variants aren't evicted by the top-K truncation.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Round-robin SA bursts** (short, 3s each) across the diverse bank instead of long     │
│                          │ single-seed slices — matches the prior architecture that scored 1.137 on the same metric. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Greedy difference-growth polish** with explicit difference-gain / sum-cost tradeoff  │
│                          │ (weight 0.35) on the global best, which is the step that actually grows |A-A| while       │
│                          │ keeping |A+A| small.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Bose-Chowla family** added as a structural seed type (it was the prior working       │
│                          │ structural prior), alongside the existing dense-core+Sidon/Golomb.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 6. **Temperature schedule**: T0=0.05, decay 0.996 every 400 steps, floor 0.0003 — slower  │
│                          │ and cooler than the current 0.12/0.97/0.001, which suits the short bursts.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 7. **Stagnation restart** kept but shortened (12s instead of 20s) since bursts are short. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes target the observed gap (1.137 -> best known 1.281) by making the seed bank │
│                          │ genuinely diverse rather than a set of near-duplicates, which the prior feedback          │
│                          │ identified as the true bottleneck.                                                        │
