│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ topk_seed_pool_with_adaptive_restart                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program's SA watchdog restarts from a freshly constructed dense-Golomb seed   │
│                          │ each time, which tends to re-enter the same basin and limits exploration. I propose       │
│                          │ introducing a persistent top-K seed pool that collects the best distinct seeds            │
│                          │ encountered during the run, and having the watchdog restart from a randomly sampled       │
│                          │ member of this pool (with occasional fresh construction to preserve diversity). This      │
│                          │ pairs richer seeding with explicit exploration pressure, matching the observation that    │
│                          │ low acceptance (~0.02–0.03) restricts exploration in prior generations.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Concretely:                                                                               │
│                          │ 1. Add a global-ish `_TOP_K` list maintained inside `_budget_adaptive_sa` (passed in/out  │
│                          │ via a mutable list argument) that keeps the K best-scoring seeds seen so far              │
│                          │ (deduplicated by a canonical tuple key).                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Change the watchdog to sample from the top-K pool with prob 0.7 and fall back to       │
│                          │ `restart_fn` otherwise. This steers restarts toward promising basins while still          │
│                          │ injecting fresh structure.                                                                │
│                          │ 3. Update `solve()` to create the pool once and pass it through all SA invocations, so    │
│                          │ learning accumulates across phases.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I keep the budget-adaptive T and the acceptance floor as-is to remain consistent with the │
│                          │ existing design and avoid regression risk; the pool mechanism is a purely additive change │
│                          │ that only affects what seed the watchdog jumps to.                                        │
