│ patch_description        │ This is a crossover between two strong solvers. From the "top-K Bose-Chowla seed bank +   │
│                          │ round-robin SA" program we keep:                                                          │
│                          │   - the single fast symmetric scorer `_score_fast` (returns both full and pure ratio),    │
│                          │   - the structured seed builders `_bose_chowla`, `_reflect`, `_build_dense_golomb`,       │
│                          │   - the round-robin SA burst `_refine_burst` (with structured rebuild moves),             │
│                          │   - the greedy difference-growth polish `_grow_by_difference`,                            │
│                          │   - the top-K seed-bank ranking by PURE ratio.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ From the "multiplicative Sidon + reflection polish" program we add:                       │
│                          │   - the reflection polish `_reflection_polish` which collapses the sum set by reflecting  │
│                          │ a tail through a chosen center,                                                           │
│                          │   - the `_prune` routine that removes elements whose removal improves the ratio,          │
│                          │   - the `_local_search` targeted SA moves (shift/add/pop/swap with ratio-aware            │
│                          │ acceptance),                                                                              │
│                          │   - the `_golomb_ruler` greedy difference-targeting builder used inside                   │
│                          │ `_build_dense_golomb`.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The combined pipeline is:                                                                 │
│                          │   Phase 1: build a broad seed bank (Bose-Chowla, scaled/reflected variants, pure          │
│                          │ intervals, dense+Golomb) and keep the top-K by PURE ratio.                                │
│                          │   Phase 2: round-robin short SA bursts across the top-K, replacing the weakest slot with  │
│                          │ any improved best.                                                                        │
│                          │   Phase 3: reflection polish on global best (new from crossover).                         │
│                          │   Phase 4: greedy difference-growth polish (difference-gain / sum-cost).                  │
│                          │   Phase 5: targeted local search (shift/add/pop/swap).                                    │
│                          │   Phase 6: prune elements that hurt the ratio.                                            │
│                          │   Phase 7: restarts with fresh structured seeds until the deadline.                       │
│                          │ This combines the seed-bank diversification of the first solver with the                  │
│                          │ reflection/pruning refinements of the second, targeting a higher combined score.          │
