                        Patch Metadata - Gen 40/1000 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                        
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ spectral_sidon_anneal                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs all rely on the same structural intuition: a dense interval (which     │
│                          │ contributes O(n²) distinct sums but also O(n²) distinct differences) glued to a           │
│                          │ Sidon/Golomb tail (which reduces the sum-set growth). I keep that structural backbone but │
│                          │ replace the local search engine with a fundamentally different one: a *spectral* /        │
│                          │ Fourier-flavored objective that rewards sets whose difference multiset concentrates       │
│                          │ energy at few frequencies while the sum set stays spread out — i.e. I directly score "few │
│                          │ sums, many differences" using a normalized additive-energy proxy rather than only         │
│                          │ counting distinct values.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Concretely:                                                                               │
│                          │ 1. I introduce `_energy_score` which computes the additive energy E(A) = #{a+b=c+d} and   │
│                          │ the difference energy D(A) = #{a-b=c-d} and uses the ratio log|A-A| / log|A+A| plus a     │
│                          │ small term proportional to (log(D/E)) to bias the search toward sets where differences    │
│                          │ are *spread* and sums are *concentrated*. This is a different signal than the plain       │
│                          │ distinct-count ratio and guides the search out of plateaus that the previous programs     │
│                          │ hit.                                                                                      │
│                          │ 2. The seed family is generalized: instead of just {i*m + i² mod m}, I use a *parametric  │
│                          │ Sidon-like* family {i*m + (i² mod m) + c*(i mod k)} which lets the search explore a       │
│                          │ continuum of Sidon-ish structures via a small integer parameter c, combining the          │
│                          │ bounded-Sidon and Golomb ideas into one tunable family.                                   │
│                          │ 3. The search itself is a *tabu + spectral hill-climb* rather than pure SA: at each step  │
│                          │ I try a small set of candidate mutations, score them with the spectral objective, and     │
│                          │ accept the best non-tabu move, with a short tabu list over the multiset of differences to │
│                          │ avoid cycling.                                                                            │
│                          │ 4. I keep the multi-phase budget structure (structured seed sweep → tabu polish →         │
│                          │ restarts) but reallocate more time to the tabu phase since the spectral objective gives a │
│                          │ stronger gradient.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result is a program that explores a different region of the search space              │
│                          │ (Sidon-parametric + spectral objective) while reusing the proven dense-core + tail        │
│                          │ scaffold.                                                                                 │
